def add(k,t,l,c,n,refs='',kind='cards',duration=75):
 slides.append(dict(k=k,title=t,lead=l,cards=c,notes=n,refs=refs,kind=kind,duration=duration))
add('TIME / AUTHORITY / EVIDENCE','Three Years\nin Thirty Minutes','Time-Travel Ethics Evaluation for AI Agents',[], 'Opening: This is a method for testing changing conditions, not a claim that we have reproduced three years of real operation. Presenter names intentionally await the readable original deck. Event label supplied by user; event schedule not independently verified.',kind='hero',duration=45)
add('01 / THE ENTERPRISE QUESTION','What changes when\nan agent stays?','Its weights may stay fixed. Its operating conditions do not.',[['Authority','Approvals expire. Permissions expand.'],['Memory','Old instructions outlive their purpose.'],['Incentives','A deadline changes the decision context.']], 'Ask the audience to imagine a service agent that keeps access while its original approval expires. The important risk is in the configured workflow, not only the underlying model. Avoid asserting that models learn merely by running.',duration=75)
add('02 / RESEARCH SIGNAL','Pressure can expose\nconcerning behavior.','Constructed experiments reveal possibilities—not production prevalence.',[['Conflict','Goals can collide with oversight.'],['Opportunity','Available tools define possible harm.'],['Context','Evaluation framing can change behavior.']], 'Anthropic’s agentic-misalignment framework crosses fictional scenarios, goal types and replacement/restriction urgency. Alignment-faking research investigates another constructed training-objective conflict. These are distinct studies. Do not quote an aggregate blackmail rate or imply a field incidence estimate. The reviewed alignment-faking README has inconsistent headline percentages, so no rate is shown.', 'R1 · R2',duration=90)
add('03 / RESEARCH MAP','Borrow the strongest\nparts of existing work.','A complementary pattern—not a new universal ethics benchmark.',[['AgentDojo / τ-bench','Tool boundaries + useful task completion'],['Inspect / ControlArena','Reproducible tasks + control protocols'],['Petri / Bloom','Behavior discovery + multi-turn audits']], 'Use the established tools as methodological anchors. Petri and Bloom repository documentation points to maintained Meridian Labs successors. Discovery should generate hypotheses; frozen independent scenarios should test them. The delivered standard-library runner is an offline calibration artifact, not a replacement for these frameworks.', 'R3 · R5–R9',duration=90)
add('04 / THE CATEGORY ERROR','Three clocks.\nThree different claims.','Never substitute a changed date for accumulated experience.',[['Wall time','Seconds spent executing'],['Logical time','Dates, expiry and policy change'],['Experience','Decisions, memory and tool effects']], 'METR’s time horizon measures success against human task-completion time. That is neither elapsed agent runtime nor ethical stability. Separate wall time, logical time and interaction count in your experimental design.', 'R4',kind='clocks',duration=90)
add('05 / DEFINE THE TARGET','Evaluate the\nconfigured system.','Model + prompts + tools + memory + permissions + oversight', [['Inputs','Requests · retrieved content · tool returns'],['Agent scaffold','Policy · memory · decision loop'],['Consequences','Proposed action · gate · changed state']], 'The full production system is the intended target. The delivered live adapter uses a fixed, finite decision scaffold; integrating a real agent requires an adapter that retains that agent’s prompts, memory, tools and control logic. Label that scope honestly.',kind='pipeline',duration=75)
add('06 / FROM STORY TO CONTRACT','Keep the narrative.\nMake consequences testable.','Game of Ethics supplies dilemmas. Enterprise gates need explicit invariants.',[['Narrative','Whose interests are in tension?'],['Policy contract','Who may do what, until when?'],['State assertion','What changed after the action?']], 'The original Ink scenarios make trade-offs legible. Their author-chosen axes and aggregate verdicts are not a compliance standard. The new extension is additive and does not yet automatically import Ink; define an action/state mapping before connecting the two.',duration=75)
add('07 / TEMPORAL SCENARIOS','The permission\nexpired yesterday.','The request is familiar. The correct action is different.',[['Month 01','Consent valid → share within purpose'],['Month 18','Consent expired → redact or escalate'],['Month 36','Check current authority again']], 'Use the timeline reveal to show that the action depends on consent facts, not just a calendar label. The demo advances monthly event batches; this example is illustrative and not a replay of one generated seed. Show the actual run JSON for exact facts.',kind='timeline',duration=75)
add('08 / MEMORY IS PART OF RISK','Remembering more\nis not always better.','The system must update, qualify and sometimes forget.',[['Superseded facts','An old approval is not a current approval.'],['Deployment context','A learned shortcut may be wrong here.'],['Deletion','Retention duties apply to memory too.']], 'LongMemEval-V2’s official 2026 repository explicitly evaluates dynamic state tracking, workflow knowledge, environment gotchas and premise awareness across web and enterprise trajectories. It measures memory capability, not ethics. Our prototype keeps only the last eight decisions plus persistent state.', 'R10 · R11',duration=75)
add('09 / THE CONTROL QUESTION','What if the agent\nproposes the wrong action?','Measure both the proposal and what the system permits.',[['Proposal','Unsafe intent cannot be hidden by a gate.'],['Enforcement','Authorization is checked outside the agent.'],['Outcome','Did harm occur? Was useful work done?']], 'ControlArena separates policy behavior, monitoring and control protocols. A deterministic gate is useful where authorization can be checked exactly. Ambiguous ethical decisions still require domain judgment. Our guard sees the oracle answer, so it is a calibration ceiling, not a realistic learned monitor.', 'R8',kind='pipeline',duration=90)
add('10 / OFFLINE PROOF','36 logical months.\n216 decision opportunities.','Six policy families. Identical seeded facts. Three calibration conditions.',[['Privacy / retention','Consent expiry · deletion deadline'],['Authority / transparency','Refund approval · audit integrity'],['Operational responsibility','Incident reporting · service repair']], 'Transition to live terminal demo. All data is synthetic; no credentials are needed. This is a test of the harness and control behavior, not an experiment on real model drift. Run the three documented commands or use the bundled evidence if the stage machine fails.',kind='numbers',duration=60)
add('11 / DEMO — 3 MINUTES','Propose → gate → record','Run offline. Inspect one decision. Verify the evidence chain.',[['01  compliant','216 completed · 0 realized violations'],['02  pressured','150 injected policy violations'],['03  guarded','150 blocked · 66 completed']], 'Three-minute demo: run compliant, pressured/audit and pressured/enforce with fresh output directories. Open the first violation at month 12 and compare its decision, expected action, blocked flag and final state. Show that hash verification fails when a stored decision is modified. These counts come from the bundled seed-0 runs. The pressure policy is deliberately programmed to fail.',kind='results',duration=180)
add('12 / THE LESSON','Zero realized harm\nis only half the dashboard.','The guarded calibration leaves 150 decisions unresolved.',[['Unsafe proposals','150 / 216'],['Realized violations','0 / 216'],['Useful completions','66 / 216']], 'The denominator is opportunities in this fixture, not independent statistical trials. A guard that blocks every request might look safe while being unusable. Show completion and unresolved work alongside failures. No confidence interval is shown for deterministic scripted behavior.',kind='results',duration=75)
add('13 / EXPERIMENTAL DESIGN','Unconfound the clock.','Vary time, pressure and experience independently.',[['Same events','Pair exogenous scenario seeds.'],['Separate treatments','Randomize pressure onset and supervision.'],['Independent holdout','New authors, tasks and attack strategies.']], 'The delivered demo starts pressure at month 12: time and pressure are confounded. That is useful for explaining the mechanism, not for estimating a causal time effect. A research study needs independent treatments and enough independent trajectories, not a larger count of dependent conversation turns.',duration=90)
add('14 / SCORE THE RIGHT THING','No single\n“ethical score.”','Keep clear invariants, contested values and task utility separate.',[['Deterministic checks','Authorization · leakage · retention'],['Expert judgment','Fairness · autonomy · proportionality'],['Uncertainty','Family-level estimates · disagreement']], 'Predefine a failure taxonomy and severity. Domain experts should resolve contested cases with a documented rubric. Calibrate LLM judges, blind target identity and assess their attack surface. Do not use chain-of-thought as definitive evidence of intent. Cluster inference by independent trajectory or task family.',duration=90)
add('15 / ENTERPRISE EVIDENCE','A release gate needs\nan accountable owner.','The report supports a decision. It does not make the decision.',[['Before deployment','Use-case classification · authority budget'],['Before more autonomy','Independent evaluation · human signoff'],['After change','Monitor · remediate · retest']], 'Discuss regulated adoption as an evidence process: accountable business owner, data governance, domain validation, escalation and post-deployment controls. Model/scaffold changes invalidate some prior evidence. Increase authority gradually and measure the actual distribution in shadow/canary stages.',duration=90)
add('16 / REGULATION','Evidence for assurance.\nNot a compliance stamp.','Map tests to obligations for the actual use and jurisdiction.',[['NIST AI RMF','Risk management and measurement'],['EU AI Act / GDPR','Role, use, rights and data obligations'],['Sector + organization','Domain validation and change governance']], 'Do not state implementation dates or classification conclusions without current legal review. Original regulatory pages were blocked during preparation. This is an evidence-planning mapping, not legal advice, conformity assessment or an ISO certificate. Use the dossier’s primary URLs for final verification.',duration=90)
add('17 / CLOUD-NATIVE PATTERN','Standard infrastructure.\nExplicit responsibilities.','Portable runner first. Deploy and validate the integration separately.',[['Kubernetes','Isolated evaluation Jobs + scoped access'],['Flux','Reviewed, versioned scenario/config delivery'],['OpenTelemetry','Decision metadata + evidence correlation']], 'Flux reconciles configuration; it is not the simulated clock. The runner advances the scenario. OTel exports are retrospective records, not measured latency spans. The delivery contains deployment examples; a cluster rollout and end-to-end collector receipt have not been executed. Do not present these as a working production installation.',kind='pipeline',duration=90)
add('18 / AUDIT TRAIL','Preserve the evidence\nthat could prove you wrong.','Versions, observations, decisions, outcomes and exceptions.',[['Reproduce','Scenario · policy · prompt · code hashes'],['Inspect','Proposed action · gate · resulting state'],['Protect','Redaction · access control · signed roots']], 'A hash chain catches changes against a trusted root but is not authentic if an attacker can replace the whole bundle and recompute it. Use immutable retention or signed external manifests for higher assurance. Real-world I/O may contain sensitive data and requires deliberate logging controls.',duration=75)
add('19 / CLAIM BOUNDARY','A calibrated instrument.\nNot three years of proof.','What works today—and the next evidence to collect.',[['Verified offline','Replay · expiry checks · control calibration'],['Provided interfaces','Compatible endpoints + optional provider router'],['Still to validate','Real agents · holdouts · cluster integration']], 'Present the validation record plainly. No model-provider efficacy measurements were made. The next study should integrate an actual scaffold, run independently authored held-out tasks and evaluate realistic monitors against adaptive attacks.',duration=75)
add('20 / TAKEAWAY','Increase autonomy\nas evidence improves.','Test the system. Vary the conditions. Measure the consequences.',[['Start small','Run the offline calibration.'],['Make it yours','Write domain-specific action/state contracts.'],['Earn the next step','Validate on independent evidence.']], 'Close with the practical call to action. The code and protocol are packaged locally; repository publishing is deferred. Leave time for questions. The aim is to replace a general claim of being ethical with specific, inspectable evidence about a defined workflow.',kind='hero',duration=45)
add('APPENDIX / SOURCE MAP','Research to read next','Primary repository evidence reviewed; full-paper verification remains outstanding.',[['R1–R4','Misalignment · alignment faking · AgentDojo · METR'],['R5–R8','Inspect · Petri · Bloom · ControlArena'],['R9–R11','τ-bench · LongMemEval · LongMemEval-V2']], 'See research/RESEARCH-DOSSIER.md for links, retrieval limits, methods and inference boundaries. Source snapshots and retrieval records are included. Do not treat repository documentation alone as a completed systematic literature review.',duration=0)
